  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWest Marshall CSD PPEL Special (September 8, 2026) - Elections - Marshall County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Marshall County | Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Marshall County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections West Marshall CSD PPEL Special\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \n2015 \n2014 \n2013 \n2012 \n2011 \n2010 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \nWest Marshall CSD PPEL Special\n\n \nSeptember 8, 2026\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Download Official Results\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n \nHighlighted Race(s) \nPublic Measure A- West Marshall CSD PPEL- Shall the Following Public Measure be Passed?\n Majority Vote for Approval · 1/1 Precincts Counted · Unofficial Results\n \n \nYes \n \n\n\n57.8%\n \n424\n \n\n \n\n \nNo \n \n\n\n42.2%\n \n309\n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \nArchived Election Details\n Absentee Vote by mail and in-person begins Wednesday, August 19th for the West Marshall CSD PPEL Special Election \n \nVoters may request an Absentee Ballot by filling out the “Official Iowa Absentee Ballot Request Form”. Forms are available at the Marshall County Auditor/Recorder’s Office, Marshall County Election Center or the Marshall County website at https://elections.marshallcountyia.gov/. \n \nTo request an absentee ballot by mail, you will need to complete the absentee ballot request form and return to our office by August 24th. \nThe In-Person absentee voting will begin on Wednesday, August 19th at the Marshall County Election Center, 107 S 1st Ave., through Friday, September 4th, between the hours of 8:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m. ID is required. \n \nMonday, September 7, 2026, the Election Center and all other County Courthouse offices will be closed for Labor Day \n \nMonday, September 7, 2026, the Election Center and all other County Courthouse offices will be closed for Labor Day \n \n\nNOTICE OF WEST MARSHALL CSD SPECIAL ELECTION \n \n\n     MARSHALL COUNTY, STATE OF IOWA \n \n\nNotice is hereby given to the qualified electors of West Marshall Community School District in the Counties of Marshall and Story in the State of Iowa, that a Special West Marshall School Election will be held on Tuesday, September 8, 2026. The polls for said election will be open from 7:00 a.m. until 8:00 p.m. Voting locations may have changed for voters for this Special Election.  Precinct Maps and Sample Ballots are available on our website https://elections.marshallcountyia.gov/ \n \n\nThe polling places shall be as follows: \n \n\nMelbourne Recreation Center- 613 Main St, Melbourne- West Marshall District Voters within Eden/Logan/Washington Precinct \n \n\nOrphan Grain Train (Clemons)- 302 Bevins St, Clemons-West Marshall District Voters within Bangor/Liscomb/Taylor & Liberty/Marietta/Minerva Precincts \n \n\nState Center City Hall- 118 E Main St, State Center- West Marshall District Voters within State Center Township Precinct \n \n\n  \n \n\nAny voter who is physically unable to enter a polling place has the right to vote in the voter’s vehicle.  For further information, please contact the Marshall County Auditor’s office at (641)754-6302 or by e-mail at election@marshallcountyia.gov   For TTY access, dial 711 + 641-754-6302. \n \n\n  \n \n\nPre-registered voters are required to provide an approved form of identification at the polling place before receiving and casting a regular ballot. Voters who are not pre-registered, such as voters registering to vote on election day and voters changing precincts, must also provide proof of residence. A voter who is unable to provide an approved form of identification (or prove residence if required) may cast a provisional ballot and provide proof of identity/residence at the county auditor’s office Monday, September 14, 2026 @ Noon. Election Day Registrants may use an attester from that precinct, but attesters must provide an approved form of identification. For additional information about providing proof of identity and/or residence visit: https://sos.iowa.gov/voterid or phone (641) 754-6302. [§49.53]   \n \n\nIn-Person absentee voting and mailed absentee voting begins August 19th. The last day to absentee vote in person is September 4th @ 5PM. In-Person absentee voting will be at the Marshall County Election Center, 107 S 1st Ave, Marshalltown. Office hours are 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM. If requesting a mailed ballot, the request form needs to be received in our office by 5 PM on August 24th. ID is Required. \n \n\nProposition A – West Marshall CSD PPEL \n \n\nShall the Following Public Measure be Adopted? \n \n\nShall the Board of Directors of the West Marshall Community School District, in the Counties of Marshall and Story, State of Iowa, for the purpose of purchasing and improving grounds; constructing schoolhouses or buildings and opening roads to schoolhouses or buildings; purchasing of buildings; purchase, lease or lease­purchase of technology and equipment; paying debts contracted for the erection or construction of schoolhouses or buildings, not including interest on bonds; procuring or acquisition of libraries; repairing, remodeling, reconstructing, improving, or expanding the schoolhouses or buildings and additions to existing schoolhouses; expenditures for energy conservation; renting facilities under Iowa Code Chapter 28E; purchasing transportation equipment for transporting students; lease purchase option agreements for school buildings or equipment; purchasing equipment authorized by law; or for any purpose or purposes now or hereafter authorized by law, be authorized for a period of ten (10) years, to levy annually, a voter-approved physical plant and equipment property tax not to exceed One Dollar ($1.00) per One Thousand Dollars ($1,000) of the assessed valuation of the taxable property within the school district commencing with the levy for collection in the fiscal year ending June 30, 2028, or each year thereafter? \n \n\nMarshall County Auditor/Recorder’s Office\n \nExtended Office Hours for Election Purposes \n \n\nMonday, August 24 - 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM at the Marshall County Election Center, 107 S 1st Ave. \n \n\nFriday, September 4 - 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM at the Marshall County Election Center, 107 S 1st Ave. \n \n\nMonday, September 7 – All County Offices are closed for Labor Day. \n \n\nElection Day, September 8 - 7:00 AM- 8:00 PM at the Marshall County Election Center, 107 S 1st Ave. \n \n\n  \n \n\nVOTER ACCESSIBLITY \n \n\nAll voting sites are fully accessible to persons with physical disabilities. Each polling place has a voter assist ballot marking device which allows persons with disabilities to vote independently. Voters may also choose another person to assist them to vote, except their employer, employer’s agent, or an officer or agent of the voter’s union. \n \n\nELECTION RESULTS\n \nResults for the West Marshall CSD Special Election will be posted on the Marshall County website: https://elections.marshallcountyia.gov. Results are not official until the final canvass is conducted on September 15, 2026. \n \n\nFor Assistance on Elections/Voter Registration/Absentee Voting\n \nContact the office of:\n \nNan Benson, Marshall County Auditor/Recorder\n \n& Commissioner of Elections\n \nMailing Address: 1 E Main St. Marshalltown, IA 50158\n \nPhone: 641-754-6302\n \nEmail: election@marshallcountyia.gov\n \nWebsite: https://elections.marshallcountyia.gov \n \n \n\n \n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n West Marshall CSD PPEL\n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Marshall County, Iowa, Elections website at elections.marshallcountyia.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Auditor/Recorder Office\n\n 1 E. Main St.\n\n Marshalltown, Iowa 50158\n\n Phone: (641) 754-6323\n\n Fax: (641) 844-2727\n\n Hours: M-F 8:00 to 4:30\n \n \nElection Center\n\n 107 S. 1st Ave.\n\n Marshalltown, IA 50158\n\n Phone: (641) 754-6302\n\n Hours: M-F 8:00 to 4:30\n\n Open for Business Twenty (20) Days Prior to Election Day\n \n \nMailing Address\n\n for the Auditor/Recorder and Elections\n\n 1 E. Main St.\n\n Marshalltown, IA 50158\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n \nContact Us •\n Accessibility •\n Marshall County Website\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
